# P5 T-U3-TCb: p5-toolgroup-retint in a session that claims truecolor
# (COLORTERM=truecolor, as p5-inline-code-retint-tc). One
# command (each product's own shell tool, in its no-questions mode) whose
# words the shell highlighter paints: a function, a string, a number, an
# operator and a comment; then the answer. Drawn dark, then the terminal
# reports light and dark again (as p5-inline-code-retint). What fx does to a
# tool row's greys on a switch -- its statusline grey, the highlighted
# words -- is what this captures.
fx: gateway p5-toolgroup-retint-fx.json
xfx: gateway p5-toolgroup-retint-xfx.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
env COLORTERM=truecolor
wait 4
type run the command
wait 1
key Enter
wait 8
snap dark
key -H 1b 5b 3f 39 39 37 3b 32 6e
wait 2
snap light
key -H 1b 5b 3f 39 39 37 3b 31 6e
wait 2
snap dark-again
